        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s1"
      },
      "text": "A post-mortem analysis of Trojan.MAC.APT28 - XAgent For the past decade, Windows users have been the main targets of consumer, for-profit cybercrime.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_7",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Bitdefender-Whitepaper-APT-Mac-A4-en-EN-web(02-23-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s6"
      },
      "text": "Since the group’s emergence in 2007, Bitdefender has become familiar with the backdoors used to compromise Windows and Linux targets, such as Coreshell, Jhuhugit and Azzy for the former OS or Fysbis for the latter.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_8",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Bitdefender-Whitepaper-APT-Mac-A4-en-EN-web(02-23-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s7"
      },
      "text": "This year we have been able to finally isolate the Mac OS X counterpart - the XAgent modular backdoor.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_10",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Bitdefender-Whitepaper-APT-Mac-A4-en-EN-web(02-23-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s1"
      },
      "text": "Context In mid-February this year, we discovered a new Mac sample that appeared to be the Mac version of the APT28 XAgent component.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_13",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Bitdefender-Whitepaper-APT-Mac-A4-en-EN-web(02-23-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s4"
      },
      "text": "Attack Flow Last year on 26 of September, PaloAlto identified a new Mac OS X Trojan associated with the APT28/Sofacy group that received the ‘Komplex’ name.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_14",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Bitdefender-Whitepaper-APT-Mac-A4-en-EN-web(02-23-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s5"
      },
      "text": "The Komplex Trojan is a binder with multiple parts: a dropper, a payload and a decoy pdf file.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_15",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
